Purpose: Build a secure, organized system to manage PrimeRoute's vehicles, drivers, rental contracts, documents, financial
transactions, maintenance, tolls, and business reporting in one coordinated workflow.
Important: Please review the scope, recommend the right architecture, and provide a phased
proposal with costs, timeline, security approach, and ongoing expenses before development
begins.
1. Project Overview
PrimeRoute needs a centralized fleet-management and business-operations system. It should be easy for employees to use,
protect confidential information, maintain reliable history, support accurate financial reporting, and scale as the fleet and
team grow.
Preferred approach: Evaluate Microsoft Access as the user interface with a secure SQL Server/Azure SQL backend. Use a
secured cloud document repository such as SharePoint for files. For full accounting, evaluate dedicated accounting software
with a planned integration rather than assuming the custom database must rebuild an entire accounting system.
The developer should recommend the best-fit architecture after confirming costs, user workflow, remote-access needs,
security requirements, and future growth.
2. Business and User Requirements
• Fleet size: 31–75+ vehicles currently/planned; design should support future growth.
• Users: 4–10 employees, including 2 administrators.
• Location: Office and remote access.
• Documents: Stored in a secured cloud repository and linked to records.
• Accounting: Full accounting needs, including accounts payable, accounts receivable, general ledger, balance sheet, and
profit-and-loss reporting. Evaluate integration with dedicated accounting software.
• Notifications: Email and text alerts.
• Platform: Microsoft Access preferred, but alternatives are acceptable if materially better for security, remote access, and
growth.
• Integrations: Not required on day one, but future connections to accounting, banking/payment services, Microsoft 365,
Excel, and e-signature tools should be considered.
• Deletion policy: Managers may delete or remove certain operational records only within defined permissions; important
financial and signed-contract history should be preserved through archiving or auditable corrections.
3. Required System Modules
A. Dashboard
• Fleet totals by status: available, reserved, rented, maintenance, unavailable, sold/retired.
• Revenue, expenses, operating profit, outstanding balances, unpaid tolls/tickets, upcoming maintenance, and expiring
documents.
• Filters for date range, vehicle, driver, and category.
B. Vehicle management
• Unique vehicle ID; VIN; license plate; make/model/year/color; mileage; purchase date and price; acquisition/financing details;
status; location; assigned driver.
• Track title, registration, insurance, purchase/finance documents, inspection reports, maintenance invoices, accident records,
warranties, and sale documents.
• Prevent duplicate VINs and preserve vehicle/driver assignment history.
C. Driver management
• Driver ID, name, contact details, license details and expiry, status, start date, current/previous rentals, payment history,
balances, inspections, accidents, tolls, tickets, and contract history.
• Restrict access to sensitive personal information and documents.
