D. Rental agreements and scheduling
• Generate a unique contract number and populate a PrimeRoute template from selected driver, vehicle, dates, rates, deposit,
mileage, and approved terms.
• Generate PDF; preserve the exact signed version; track draft, awaiting signature, active, renewed, terminated, and
completed statuses.
• Support extensions/amendments and prevent overlapping vehicle assignments.
• Flag vehicles under maintenance or otherwise unavailable.
E. Revenue, payments, and driver balances
• Record rental charges separately from payments received, deposits, refunds, credits, adjustments, and outstanding
balances.
• Track dates, methods, references, due dates, payment status, and receipts.
• Generate driver statements, receipts, overdue reports, and collection reports.
F. Expense management
• Record date, category, vehicle, related driver/contract, vendor, description, amount, payment method/status, invoice/receipt,
entered-by, approver, and notes.
• Categories include insurance, registration, oil changes, repairs, tires, towing, cleaning, tolls, parking, tickets, marketing,
software, bank fees, office, legal/accounting, and other costs.
• Include approvals, duplicate invoice warnings, and auditable corrections.
G. Vehicle profitability
• Report rental revenue, operating expenses, insurance, maintenance, repairs, financing costs, depreciation where applicable,
rental days, downtime, revenue/cost per rental day, and lifetime performance.
• Clearly distinguish cash flow, operating profit, and accounting profit; confirm accounting rules with PrimeRoute's accountant.
H. Tolls, tickets, and citations
• Track vehicle, driver during the relevant rental period, contract, issuing authority, reference number, incurred/received dates,
amount, due date, payment proof, driver charge/recovery, balance, and status.
• Support review before assigning responsibility or charging a driver; report overdue and unresolved items.
I. Maintenance and oil changes
• Track service date, odometer, service type, provider, cost, invoice, next service mileage/date, and status.
• Support a 5,000-mile oil-change interval or another interval set by PrimeRoute/manufacturer guidance.
• Send due/overdue alerts and allow authorized users to mark a vehicle unavailable.
J. Inspections, damage, and accidents
• Pickup and return inspections: mileage, fuel, interior/exterior condition, existing/new damage, photos, date/time, inspector,
and driver acknowledgment.
• Link damage to estimates, repair invoices, insurance claims, deductible terms, driver charges (where applicable), amounts
recovered, and resolution.
K. Insurance and compliance
• Track insurer, policy, coverage, premium, deductible, effective/expiry dates, documents, claims, and contacts.
• Alert on expiring insurance, registration, licenses, contracts, and other required documents.
