statements; receivables/payables; utilization/downtime; maintenance; tolls/tickets; document expiry; contract expiry; vendor
spending.
• Authorized export to PDF/Excel; consider Power BI for advanced analytics.
4. Accounting and Financial Controls
• PrimeRoute needs full accounting capabilities: accounts payable, accounts receivable, general ledger, balance sheet, and
profit-and-loss reporting.
• Please propose whether to integrate a dedicated accounting platform (for example, QuickBooks Online or an equivalent)
rather than custom-building a complete accounting engine.
• Define how charges, invoices, payments, deposits, refunds, vendor bills, and adjustments will flow between systems without
double counting.
• A refundable security deposit must not automatically be treated as rental revenue.
• Vehicle purchase costs, loan principal, interest, and depreciation must be treated correctly under the accounting method
approved by PrimeRoute's accountant.
• Provide reconciliation procedures and reports that allow financial transactions to be traced back to the original record.
