7. Alerts and Automation
• Email and text alerts for overdue payments, upcoming contract endings, expiring licenses/registration/insurance, oil changes,
maintenance, unpaid tolls/tickets, missing documents, unresolved accidents, and vehicles awaiting inspection.
• Configurable lead times, recipients, and alert status to prevent unnecessary repeated messages.
• Keep a history of important alerts and whether they were resolved.
8. Database Design and Data Integrity
• Use a normalized relational design with unique IDs, appropriate relationships, validation, and referential integrity.
