• Accounting software recommendation and integration scope.
• Remote access and mobile-phone support options.
• How PrimeRoute will own and control its data, accounts, files, and source code.
• Training, warranty, maintenance, support response times, and future change-request pricing.
• Relevant experience with fleet/rental systems, accounting workflows, and secure multiuser applications.
13. Items to Confirm During Discovery
• Current accounting software, if any.
• Whether employees must use the system on phones for photos, inspections, and receipts.
• Whether weekly rental charges should be generated automatically.
• Which expense/payment amounts require manager or second-administrator approval.
• Whether a browser/mobile application is required at launch or only a future option.
• Exact contract templates, policies, financial categories, notification lead times, and document-retention rules.
Project success standard
A secure, maintainable system owned and controlled by PrimeRoute that provides reliable
fleet, rental, document, and financial records; restricts employee access appropriately;
preserves audit history; and can scale as the business grows.
